        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Low lumbar pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Daytime pain is about the same, a mild ache that increases with prolonged sitting at a desk. For the past 3–4 weeks, more aware of pain at night when trying to sleep. Localized to the low lumbar area, right greater than left; non-radicular. Dull ache with occasional sharp twinge on extension or twisting in bed."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep onset and waking"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Takes longer to fall asleep and wakes 1–2 times to change position, then returns to sleep. Sleep onset delay attributed to pain; late caffeine and mattress may also contribute."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
